On Tuesday 22 June 2004 11:12 Jakob Creutzig
(creutzig@mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de) wrote:

> Hmmh.. Never tried, but would genociding a pet be
> counted as killing it for alignment purposes?

It doesn't; it's the same as if a monster kills it or it has an accident
not caused by the player.

> Anyhow, I don't know exactly when a pet on a
> different level is viewed as no-longer-pet by
> the game internals; most likely this will be
> updated continuously, not at the time you
> hit the same level again.

It's in fact *updated* when you hit the same level again, but the time
the pet has been away from you is taken into account then. For all
practical purposes, when your pet is not on the same level as you it
doesn't exist. It doesn't come when you blow your magic whistle, after
all (<YANI alert> perhaps there's a calling for blessed magic whistles
there</>).

